144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Templates over GPT-2 - GPT-2 was tested and produced hallucinations. For a career guidance tool where a wrong recommendation has real consequences, reliability matters more than generative variety. A harder decision than it sounds - it means every strong-fit candidate receives structurally identical output.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Single-agent ReAct over multi-agent - Sequential execution keeps the reasoning trace legible and the state dictionary simple. The tradeoff is latency - tools cannot run in parallel. Acceptable for a career orientation tool where session time is not critical.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Keyword taxonomy over NER - The 50-skill taxonomy is interpretable and debuggable. A trained NER model would have higher coverage but lower transparency. Given the EU AI Act requirement for explainability in recruitment AI, interpretability was prioritised. The coverage gap is the biggest known limitation.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 83 0 R
/Pg 15 0 R
/A [271 0 R 0]
/K [6]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Ethical Considerations and Responsible AI)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Recruiter misuse is the primary risk. Similarity scores designed to guide candidates could be repurposed to rank or filter applicants - encoding the biases in 80% UK and German training data into hiring decisions. The mitigation is architectural: no recruiter-facing interface exists, and the responsible use boundary is documented across all project artefacts.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Overconfident output is the second risk. The system says "your profile aligns strongly with..." based on a 50-keyword match with no uncertainty quantification. The mitigation is the full reasoning trace included in every report - candidates see exactly what was detected and why - and explicit framing as a first-pass orientation tool, not a definitive career assessment.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (EU AI Act classifies recruitment AI as high-risk under Annex III, with compliance enforceable from August 2026. EACIS was designed to meet these requirements from the outset - session isolation, explainable reasoning traces and no recruiter interface eliminate the highest-risk deployment scenarios before they can occur.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 84 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/A [272 0 R 0]
/K [4]
>>
endobj
